From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000198 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: add disabled MT6797 BigiDVFS readback

The retained MT6797 secure-owner audit identifies one read-only secure
register service, REG_READ at 0xc200035f, and four exact BigiDVFS register
addresses. It does not prove that the header-advertised PLL getter FIDs are
implemented by the target firmware, so do not call them merely because they
exist in a public header.

Expose only the proven, read-only service behind a disabled platform node. The
driver accepts the four exact addresses, rejects every other address, treats
unknown or sign-extended secure returns as a sticky fault, and serializes a
complete raw-register sample. It never calls a secure write or state-changing
FID, does not derive an OPP or voltage table, and does not register a
BigiDVFS state owner or clock provider.

This is an experiment-only transport and is not submission-ready.
---
